Implementation looks good. However, I don't agree with the change. 

The reason is, this change will force users to always overwrite vertex color with texture color. However, there are plenty of valid use cases where the user may intend access the vertex-color rather than the texture color.

For example, consider a shader that chooses a texture based on vertex color
```
void fragment() {
    COLOR = mix(texture_a, texture_b, COLOR.r);
}
```
The above shader would mix between ``texture_a`` and ``texture_b`` based off ``texture(TEXTURE, UV).r`` rather than ``COLOR.r`` coming from the vertex shader. 

If I have misunderstood how this change will work, please let me know.

